  "feedback_interpretation": "Round-three measurements strengthened the high-ratio underprediction signal for naphthylmethanol (55.82/113.21 mL measured at 10/1) and methoxybenzaldehyde (56.20/117.46 mL at 50/1). Iodophenol at 20/1 measured 26.27/49.10 mL against 41.29/70.41 mL predicted, reversing the earlier 50/1 error direction. Fluorobenzonitrile at 50/1 measured 24.86/44.05 mL against 14.76/33.29 mL predicted, unlike the early-eluting methylbenzonitriles. These results motivated matched-ratio probes and structural contrasts. Initial L333 records were used as measured anchors only, without assigning them out-of-sample prediction errors.",
